{"seq":12,"trial_id":"company-brain-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-company-scoped-mu-heldout/ho-04-hartford-summary/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-25T01:06:49.684Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"55820b04b9beef6766edff6cb827963629d4e1cadbccd2d0dcdaf8f2f742db29","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1X6KN92LKD","text":"Gideon, here's the draft for Mateo's procurement team. I checked #inc-vtg-hartford directly, and it matches the ticket record. It has no finance figures.\n\n**Hartford gate kiosks outage, 3 Aug 2026 (SUP-5380 / INC-4821)**\n\n- **First report:** Sev 1 ticket SUP-5380 was logged at 08:12, with drivers queuing after a failed reboot. The incident room's first update came at 10:42, after the lanes showed a white screen following badge scans.\n- **Impact:** Both inbound lanes were down. Check-in moved to paper trailer numbers. Six trucks queued at the east gate, and the door 14 resin delivery was at risk before the afternoon shift.\n- **Kiosk 1 back:** 11:03. The guard checked in trailer 8836 and dispatch saw it.\n- **Both lanes confirmed working:** 11:07.\n- **Still open:** Mateo's status-page login is still being fixed (screenshot on INC-4821). Kiosk 2 stays powered on for Carrowmere Cloud's reconnect logs.\n\nTwo things to confirm before this goes out:\n- The \"first report\" is 08:12 on the ticket, not 10:42 in the channel. Tell me if procurement should see the 10:42 time instead.\n- Your 11:08 post said \"leaving this open,\" so the incident may still be open. I've written it that way.\n\nI haven't emailed or posted this anywhere else. If you want it sent to Mateo or his team, tell me who and I'll check the directory first."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1X6KN92LKD","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
